of durable `agent_run_events` with a gapless handoff to live delivery, single-owner authorization, and ephemeral `message_update` deltas chunked and sent only over `semprec_agent_stream` without being persisted. This step addressed the last outstanding review finding: the `2026-09-12-per-process-agent-run-watch-registry` ADR now cross-references the structurally parallel `2026-09-12-per-process-doc-sync-subscription-registry` ADR from issue #162, so the similarity between the two per-process registries is explicit rather than left for a reader to notice independently. The other three previously-open findings (an `@semprec/data` re-export ADR violation, a replay-replacement race that could drop an established watcher on a transient DB error, and duplicated UUID/event-id validation helpers) were already fixed in earlier commits on this branch. Verified before pushing: backend `pnpm run verify` (lint, typecheck, build, migrations, 94 test files / 1152 tests, e2e suite) and web `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 18 test files / 139 tests) — all green. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-13 05:09Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #395 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed to branch `bb/relay-163-realtime-v1-04-06-replay-and-stream-wa-thr_hssukzn4cs` (backing open PR #395). ## Summary Implements `agent:watch`/`agent:unwatch` for issue #163: cursor-based replay of durable `agent_run_events` with a gapless handoff to live delivery, single-owner authorization, and ephemeral `message_update` deltas chunked and sent only over `semprec_agent_stream` without being persisted. This round addressed all 3 low-severity findings from the latest review pass: - `deliver()` in `agentRunWatch.ts` was declared `async` with no `await` in its body — made it synchronous, removing an unnecessary Promise allocation on every event delivery. - `publishAgentRunDelta`'s fast (unchunked) path let `JSON.stringify` silently drop an explicit `undefined` delta, which `parseAgentStreamMessage` then rejected for missing the `delta` key — normalized to `null` before serializing. - `realtime.test.ts`'s `wireRealtimeHooks` tests each only reset the one hook they exercised — extracted a shared `resetHooks()` helper so the newest test can't leave other hooks wired to the pool for a later test to trip over. Verified before pushing: backend `pnpm run verify` (lint, typecheck, build, migrations, 94 test files / 1152 tests, e2e suite) and web `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 18 test files / 139 tests) — all green. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-13 08:32Z — This issue was resolved by #395, which just merged into develop.",
